- Current readiness probe: `http-get http://:80/readyz`
- nginx doesn't serve `/readyz`, so it returns 404

I need to change the path from `/readyz` to something nginx serves. Common options:
1. `/health` - standard health check endpoint (but not all nginx configs have this)
2. `/` or `""` - root path which always serves nginx default page

Looking at nginx documentation, the most reliable option is just using an empty path or `/`. The simplest fix is to change `/readyz` to an empty string or just `/`.

Let me construct a patch that changes the readiness probe path:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "readinessProbe": {
              "httpGet": {
                "path": "/"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

